📌 What is a Namespace?
A namespace is a logical separation inside a Kubernetes cluster that groups resources together.

Resource Isolation
Different teams, projects, or environments can have their own namespaces.

Name Uniqueness
Namespaces allow you to reuse resource names.
Example:
You can have two Services both named frontend in different namespaces:
	• dev/frontend
	• prod/frontend


Resource Quotas
You can limit CPU, memory, and object counts per namespace.


